{:id "0008-engine-isolation"
 :title "Scout's engine runs with no tools at all, and the persona as its system prompt"
 :lupa/deps #{"0005-worker"}
 :lupa/area :agent
 :lupa/risk :high
 :goal "The agent can only talk. Today the :claude engine runs `claude -p`
        with the host session's defaults: the built-in file and shell tools,
        and every MCP connector the host has (in the foreman's session that
        was 40 Gmail, Calendar and Drive tools), so anyone in a conversation
        could ask the agent to read files or mail on the worker's machine.
        After this order the engine disables every tool, and the persona is
        the system prompt rather than text in the user turn."
 :scope ["src/halfahead/worker/core.clj" "src/halfahead/worker/engine.clj"
         "test/halfahead/worker/core_test.clj" "test/halfahead/worker/engine_test.clj"]
 :design "worker.core: split engine-prompt into two public pure fns:
            (engine-system-prompt request) -> the persona, a blank line, and
              the answering instructions (the JSON shape and the five
              deliveries, exactly as engine-prompt has them today)
            (engine-transcript request) -> the transcript lines ('Human:' /
              'You:') ending with 'You:'
          Keep engine-prompt as their concatenation (system, blank line,
          transcript) for engines that take one string (:mock).

          worker.engine: claude-command returns
            [\"claude\" \"-p\" transcript
             \"--system-prompt\" system
             \"--tools\" \"\"
             \"--disallowedTools\" \"mcp__*\"
             \"--output-format\" \"json\"]
          Define the two isolation flags in one private var with a comment
          saying why (built-in tools and inherited MCP connectors), so they
          cannot be dropped by accident. Nothing else changes."
 :acceptance
 ["claude-command's vector contains, in order, \"--tools\" \"\" and
   \"--disallowedTools\" \"mcp__*\", and passes the system prompt via
   --system-prompt and the transcript as the -p argument"
  "The -p argument does not contain the persona text; the --system-prompt
   argument does, followed by the five delivery names"
  "engine-system-prompt and engine-transcript are pure, tested, and their
   concatenation equals engine-prompt"
  "The existing worker tests still pass unchanged; `bb test` stays green"]
 :non-goals
 ["Do not edit halfahead.schema, store, or main"
  "No new engines; no API-key engine (that needs a key the founder has
   not provided)"]
 :context ["src/halfahead/worker/core.clj" "src/halfahead/worker/engine.clj"
           "test/halfahead/worker/engine_test.clj" "DESIGN.md"]
 :budget-usd 6.0}
